comment.body:
Thanks for the report. Workspaces Capture already filters some window types by design (for example certain popup/untitled windows and some elevated windows when PowerToys is not running elevated), so before we chase code changes, could you please provide:
1. the exact app names/processes that were visible but missing from Capture;
2. whether each missing window was minimized, running as administrator, or hosted inside another app such as Edge/Chrome;
3. whether PowerToys itself was running as administrator when you used Add Workspace > Capture; and
4. whether the request for manually adding an app to an existing workspace is a separate feature ask from the missing-capture bug.
That will tell us whether this is an unsupported window class, a privilege limitation, or a reproducible capture bug.
